Guard the failed-pod Terminated reason rewrite in checkPodsStatus.

When every remotely reported container has terminated and one of them failed,
checkPodsStatus rewrote State.Terminated.Reason on every in-cluster container
status. A status the plugin did not report (for example a container excluded
from offloading) is still Waiting or Running, so its Terminated is nil and the
virtual kubelet panics with a nil dereference while holding podsMu, which
crash-loops the node. Only statuses that are terminated are rewritten now.

Upstream status: reported to interlink-hq/interLink in a drafted issue, not
yet filed (see readme).

